# Key shortcuts the GUI harness's window manager keeps (#1209).
#
# matchbox's stock /etc/matchbox/kbdconfig grabs Alt+n, Alt+p, Alt+c, Alt+d
# and Alt+m on the whole display. Journeys that lost exactly one `p` while
# typing ("Alha", "aple", "ket", "lain", "oaqueedit") are all a dropped `p`,
# and Alt+p is the one letter binding that would eat it were Alt ever seen as
# held. A window manager that grabs letter keys has no place under a test
# that types them, so only the bindings below remain: the ones that do not
# take a letter.
<alt>f4=close
f11=fullscreen
